OSPF_TC88.steps:
Enable packet monitor on Sonicwall;
2. Configure interface X3, zone LAN, static IP, connect to router, enable OSPF on sonicwall and router, area 0;
3. Check the packets transmits between sonicwall and router, sonicwall send all types of OSPF messages, e.g. hello, DD, LSR, LSU...
4. Disable OSPF on X3, check the packets transmits between sonicwall and router, sonicwall must not send any OSPF messages.

Declare_TC90.steps:
Enable packet monitor on Sonicwall;
2. Configure interface X3, zone LAN, static IP, connect to router, enable OSPF on sonicwall area 0;
3. Enable OSPF on router, area 0;
4. Check the packets transmits between sonicwall and router, in the first 40 seconds, sonicwall send hello message and does not declare DR or BDR in the hello message, wait for 40 seconds, it start declare itself as the DR in its hello message

DeadInterval_TC91.steps:
Configure interface X3, zone LAN, static IP, connect to router, enable OSPF on sonicwall and router, area 0;
2. Verify sonicwall and router can establish neighbor with each other;
3. Use command "show ip ospf neighbor" on sonicwall to check the neighbor list on sonicwall;
4. Disable OSPF on router, wait about 40, use command "show ip ospf neighbor" on sonicwall to check the neighbor list on sonicwall;

RouterPrior_TC93.steps:
Prepare two routers, sonicwall and router;
2. Connect sonicwall X3 to router;
3. Configure sonicwall X3, zone LAN, static IP 28.1.1.46;
4. Enable packet monitor on sonicwall;
5. Enable OSPF on X3 , router priority is 0, enable OSPF on router too, router priority is 0, router is 28.1.1.55, area 0;
6. Wait about 1 min, check the packets transmit between sonicwall and router, sonicwall send hello packet every 10 seconds, but at last, neither doesn't declare it as DR nor BDR;
7, Use command "show ip ospf neighbor" in CLI in sonicwall, the sonicwall and router's OSPF status stay in 2-way state.

HelloMismatch_TC96.steps:
Prepare 2 routers, sonicwall , router;
2. Configure interface X3 on sonicwall, zone LAN, static IP 28.1.1.46, connect to router, router has static IP 28.1.1.55;
3. Enable packet monitor on sonicwall;
4. Enable OSPF on sonicwall X3, area 0, keep other settings as default;
5. Enable OSPF on router , set hello-interval to 5 seconds, area 0;
6. Check the packets received and send sonicwall X3, sonicwall received hello message send from router, the hello-interval is 5 seconds, but sonicwall does not accept router as its active neighbor in its hello message;
7. Use command "show ip ospf neighbor" in CLI in sonicwall, check the neighbor list is blank.

DiffIP_TC97.steps:
Configure sonicwall interface X3, zone LAN, static IP 28.1.1.46/24, connect to a router , router has static IP 55.1.1.1/24;
2. Enable OSPF on interface X3 in sonicwall, area 0;
3. Enable OSPF on router, area 0;
4. Enable packet monitor on sonicwall;
5. Check the packets received and send on sonicwall, sonicwall received hello message from router, but it does not add the router into its active neighbor in the hello message send by sonicwall;
6. Use command "show ip ospf neighbor" in CLI in sonicwall, check the neighbor list is blank.

EBit_TC98.steps:
Configure sonicwall interface X3, zone LAN, static IP 28.1.1.46/24, connect to a router , router has static IP 28.1.1.28/24;
2. Enable OSPF on interface X3 in sonicwall, area 0, normal area type;
3. Enable packet monitor on sonicwall;
4. Check the hello packet send from sonicwall, the E bit of the Options field in a Hello packet must be set to match this area's ExternalRoutingCapability;
5. Change OSPF area type from normal to stub in sonicwall, check the hello packets again, the E-bit must be clear in sended Hello Packets.

MasterSlave_TC101.steps:
Configure interface X3, zone LAN, static IP address 28.1.1.85, enable OSPF on interface X3, connect to a router, router's IP 28.1.1.28, enable OSPF on router too, both in area 0;
2. Change sonicwall ospf router-id to 28.1.1.5, other router's router-id is 28.1.1.28, clear ip ospf process on sonicwall and router, meanwhile, enable packet monitor on sonicwall;
3. Check the packets transmit between sonicwall and router, check packet of DB Description, at first, sonicwall and router send DB Description packet to each other and set the M/S bit to 1, with different DD sequence numbers, e.g. sonicwall use DD sequence number 100, router use DD sequence number 200;
4. Then sonicwall send another DB Description, respond to router's DB Description, with DD sequence number 200, and set M/S bit to 0.

MasterSlave_TC102.steps:
Configure interface X3, zone LAN, static IP address 28.1.1.85, enable OSPF on interface X3, connect to a router, router's IP 28.1.1.28, enable OSPF on router too, both in area 0;
2. Change sonicwall ospf router-id to 28.1.1.85, other router's router-id is 28.1.1.28, clear ip ospf process on sonicwall and router, meanwhile, enable packet monitor on sonicwall;
3. Check the packets transmit between sonicwall and router, check packet of DB Description, at first, sonicwall and router send DB Description packet to each other and set the M/S bit to 1, with different DD sequence numbers, e.g. sonicwall use DD sequence number 100, router use DD sequence number 200;
4. Then router send another DB Description, respond to sonicwall's DB Description, with DD sequence number 100, and set M/S bit to 0.

VLAN_TC117.steps:
Add a vlan sub-interface, parent interface X3, zone LAN, vlan id 100, static IP 67.67.67.2/24, connect to a router g0/0.100, router g0/0.100 has static IP 67.67.67.1/24;
2. Enable OSPF on sonicwall X3:V100 and router g0/0.100, area 0, enable redistribute static routes on both sonicwall and router;
3. Verify that OSPF status between sonicwall and router 2, the status from Loading to FULL;
4. Check Sonicwall's routing table, it can learn static routes from router via X3:V100;
5. Use command "show ip ospf route" on router to check the router's ospf routing table, it can learn static routes from Sonicwall via g0/0.100.

VLAN_TC117.result:
in step 3, the OSPF LED status becomes GREEN;
in step 4, check the sonicwall's routing table, the static routes learned from router via X3:V100 appeared on the routing table;
in step 5, router can learn static routes from Sonicwall via the vlan interface.

VLAN_TC118.steps:
Add a vlan sub-interface, parent interface X3, zone LAN, vlan id 100, static IP 67.67.67.2/24, connect to a router g0/0.100, router g0/0.100 has static IP 67.67.67.1/24;
2. Enable OSPF on sonicwall X3:V100 and router g0/0.100, area 0, enable redistribute static routes on both sonicwall and router;
3. Verify that OSPF status between sonicwall and router 2, the status from Loading to FULL;
4. Check Sonicwall's routing table, it can learn static routes from router via X3:V100;
5. Use command "show ip ospf route" on router to check the router's ospf routing table, it can learn static routes from Sonicwall via g0/0.100;
6. Back to interface page, attempt to delete this newly added vlan sub-interface X3:V100, it must failed, GUI prompt error message "Index of the interface.: Interface is in use by OSPF ";
7, Disable OSPF on interface X3:V100, attempt to delete this interface again, it will be succeed.

VLAN_TC118.result:
in step 3, the OSPF LED status becomes GREEN;
in step 4, check the sonicwall's routing table, the static routes learned from router via X3:V100 appeared on the routing table;
in step 5, router can learn static routes from Sonicwall via the vlan interface.
in step 6, this added vlan sub-interface can not be deleted when OSPF is enabled on it, GUI should prompt "Error: Index of the interface.: Interface is in use by OSPF ";
in step 7, after OSPF is disabled on this vlan sub-interface, then this vlan sub-interface could be succeed to be deleted.

OSPF_TC119.steps:
Add a static route, dst to 202.55.12.0/24, with reachable gateway and outgoing interface;
2. Configure interface X3, zone LAN, static IP address 28.1.1.46, enable OSPF on interface X3, connect to a router, router's IP 28.1.1.28, enable OSPF on router too, both in area 0;
3. Turned on check box "Redistribute Static Routes" on sonicwall X3, with metric 4646, tag 4600;
4. Verify Sonicwall and router established OSPF neighborhood, OSPF status change from Loading to FULL;
5. Use command "show ip ospf route" to check the router's ospf routing table, the static route dst to 202.55.12.0/24 must appear in router's ospf routing table with correct metric and tag.

ALLRouting_TC124.steps:
when routing mode is advanced mode, enable RIP , OSPF, BGP on sonicwall, and connect sonicwall to router;
2. Make sure sonicwall can establish RIP , OSPF, BGP neighborhood with router;
3. Transit to simple routing mode, and transit back to advanced routing mode;
4. After transition, all RIP, OSPF , BGP configurations are keep intact, sonicwall will rebuild RIP and OSPF neighborhood with router, the BGP will be disabled after transtion, so enable BGP on GUI, verify Sonicwall can establish neighbor with router again.

TransMode_TC125.steps:
Configure interface X1, zone WAN, static mode, ip 10.8.153.153/24;
2. Configure interface X5, zone LAN, transparent mode, transparent range 10.8.153.200-10.8.153.230;
3. Navigate to Network->Routing, click edit button of X5's RIP and OSPF, all of them can not be enabled on X5, it is gray and prompt it is a transparent I/F.

VPN_TC152.steps:
Add site to site VPN policy on local and remote FW, and use an AO Group as the local and remote network;
Enable OSPF/RIP on DUT, redistribute the remote VPN network;
Use command "show ip route ospf" on router;
Disable site to site VPN policy, check router "show ip route ospf".

VPN_TC152.result:
in step 1, make sure the VPN policy is established;
in step 2, make sure OSPF neighbor established;
in step 3, make sure router learned the remote VPN network from DUT;
in step 4, make sure when the VPN is down, the remote VPN network routes disappeared on router.
